          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of
            %em pushout product
            is a natural kind of pairing operation on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            equipped with a pairing operation on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            (e.g. a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            of the
            = succeed "-diagram" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            objects. Regarding arrows in a category as diagrams with domain the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+category"} interval category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            with the natural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} copowering
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            replacing a tensor in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} coend
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p Consider
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                three
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℰ
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_i
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \{1,2,3\}
              %p (often taken to be the same),
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes \colon \mathcal{E}_1 \times \mathcal{E}_2 \to \mathcal{E}_3
                out of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
              %p
                (often being the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
                or the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
                of an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
                over its
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmos"} cosmos
          %p
            Assume that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_3
            has all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℰ
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_1
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon X \to Y
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℰ
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_2
            %p
              their
              %strong pushout product
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_3
