            %p where the top row is the unique map on the initial object by assumption whence its pushout to the bottom horizontal morphism is also an identity, as shown.
          %p
          #PushoutProductWithAnIdentity.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (pushout product with identity is identity morphism)
              %br/
              With respect to any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifunctor"} bifunctor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ×
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes \,\colon\, \mathcal{C} \times \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
              is an identity morphism:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi id
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi id
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext and
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi id
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi id
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \,\widehat{\otimes}\, id
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    id
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\text{and}
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    id \,\widehat{\otimes}\, g
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    id
                    \\,.
            %p
